{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetBPqWA4YczKpiwDyYRM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent, baseline tests pass. Now I have all the information I need for the analysis.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — current endpoints are `POST /shipments` (create), `GET /shipments/{shipmentId}` (get), `GET /shipments` (list). No confirm endpoint.\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — data class with `shipmentId`, `orderId`, `carrier`, `status` fields.\n- `ShipmentStatus:23-27` — enum with `CREATED`, `CONFIRMED`, `CANCELLED` values.\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — in-memory store with `save`, `findById`, `existsById`, `findAll`, `clear` methods.\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — `ResourceNotFoundException` maps to 404, `ConflictException` maps to 409.\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — `ErrorCode` enum with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`, `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`, but no code for invalid state transitions.\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — centralizes exception handling; all `ApiException` subtypes turned into error envelopes.\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:1-84` — tests create, get, list, and error cases. No state transition tests.\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Error responses use a standard envelope with `error.code`, `error.message`, and `error.fields` (from `ApiError` and `GlobalExceptionHandler`).\n2. Status-changing endpoints throw `ApiException` subclasses (`ResourceNotFoundException` for 404, `ConflictException` for 409).\n3. Controllers inject repositories and perform simple CRUD + validation logic.\n4. Tests use `MockMvc` with `post()`, `get()`, status assertions, and `jsonPath()` for response body checks.\n5. The testing-and-verification skill emphasizes: assert response bodies (not just status), use separate `GET` requests to verify state changes, test repeats/idempotency, and assert error codes not just status.\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — **Must change** to add error code for when a shipment is in an invalid state for confirmation (e.g., already cancelled).\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — **Must change** to add the `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint.\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — **Must change** to add tests for the confirm endpoint, including success, idempotent repeat, cancelled rejection, and not-found cases.\n\n**Risks:**\n- The new error code for invalid state transitions needs to fit the existing `ErrorCode` enum without breaking the API contract.\n- The confirm logic must properly handle the idempotent case (confirming an already-confirmed shipment must succeed).\n- The repository's `save()` method returns a new object, so the controller must return the updated shipment from the response body.\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket clearly defines all four cases and their expected HTTP status/behavior.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`:** Add a new `ErrorCode` enum value called `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to represent when a shipment cannot transition to the requested state (specifically, when confirming a cancelled shipment). This keeps error codes stable and machine-readable.\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`:** Add a new method `confirm(shipmentId: String)` decorated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Fetches the shipment by ID; throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found (404).\n   - If status is `CREATED`, transition to `CONFIRMED`, save, and return 200 with the updated shipment.\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, return 200 with the unchanged shipment (idempotent, no save needed).\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` (409).\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`:** Add five test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and persists it` — POST confirm on `CREATED` shipment, assert 200 and `CONFIRMED` in response, then GET the shipment and verify it is persisted as `CONFIRMED`.\n   - `confirm on already confirmed shipment succeeds without change` — POST confirm twice on same shipment, assert both are 200, assert second response is identical to first, GET and verify no change.\n   - `confirm on cancelled shipment is rejected with 409` — Write a `CANCELLED` shipment directly to the repository, POST confirm, assert 409 and `error.code = SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS`, GET and verify shipment is still `CANCELLED`.\n   - `confirm on unknown shipment is rejected with 404` — POST confirm on non-existent ID, assert 404 and `error.code = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`.\n   - (The fifth test is the repeat/idempotent case mentioned above.)\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered keeping the same error code as `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` for both \"duplicate on create\" and \"trying to confirm a cancelled shipment.\" I rejected this because the error codes document what went wrong, and these are two distinct problems: one is a conflict in the create domain (duplicate ID), the other is a conflict in the state transition domain (invalid status). Two problems need two codes.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Response | Status |\n|------|-------|------|-------|----------|--------|\n| Happy path (CREATED→CONFIRMED) | shipmentId | findById(shipmentId), status=CREATED | save(Shipment{status=CONFIRMED}) | Shipment{status=CONFIRMED} | 200 |\n| Idempotent (already CONFIRMED) | shipmentId | findById(shipmentId), status=CONFIRMED | (none) | Shipment{status=CONFIRMED} | 200 |\n| Error: not found | shipmentId | findById(shipmentId)=null | (none) | error{code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND} | 404 |\n| Error: cancelled | shipmentId | findById(shipmentId), status=CANCELLED | (none) | error{code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS} | 409 |\n\nAll errors are thrown as `ApiException` subclasses, caught by `GlobalExceptionHandler`, and serialized into the standard error envelope.\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Happy path:** Create a shipment (auto-CREATED), call confirm, assert 200 + `CONFIRMED` in body, then GET and assert persisted as `CONFIRMED`. Covers acceptance criterion 3.\n2. **Idempotent repeat:** Confirm twice on the same shipment, assert both 200, assert bodies match, GET and verify no change. Covers acceptance criterion 5 (repeated confirm succeeds).\n3. **Cancelled rejection:** Write a `CANCELLED` shipment to repository, POST confirm, assert 409 + `error.code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS`. Covers acceptance criterion 5 (cancelled shipment is refused) and criterion 4 (error responses consistent).\n4. **Not found:** POST confirm on unknown ID, assert 404 + `error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`. Covers acceptance criterion 5 (unknown id is refused).\n5. **Ensure no regression:** All existing tests pass unchanged. Covers acceptance criteria 1 & 2.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the three required changes.\n\n**Step 1: Add the error code to `ApiError.kt`**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1465,"cache_read_input_tokens":20772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1465},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cf2c24cc-dd01-4784-aaac-304aa3fb9c0b","uuid":"96596e65-263d-4ce6-8feb-270799fd1cf3","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:27:55.779Z","request_id":"req_011CetBPprxJAodXerYtdoWK"}
